  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Canicross 83 is a club affiliated with the Fédération des Sports et Loisirs Canins (FSLC - French dog sports and leisure federation), with group training sessions in the Tourves/Bras and Cuers areas. Several disciplines are offered: canicross, cani-mountain-biking, cani-walking/jogging, cani-hiking and ski-joring, so you can find the format that suits you and your dog.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Training sessions take place on Wednesdays and Fridays in the Tourves/Bras area, and on Wednesdays plus either Monday or Friday in the Cuers area. The schedule is published every Sunday evening on Facebook and Instagram. A discovery pass offers 3 free trial sessions for beginners, supervised by certified instructors (BAF1/BAF2). The club also organises competitions, including "Canicross en Provence Verte". Membership is through a club form followed by a licence on the federation's platform (courses.ffslc.fr), over a season running from 1 September to 31 August; the exact membership fee is not published online — ask the club directly.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: take advantage of the discovery pass to try the discipline before committing, and remember to check the schedule published every Sunday evening before heading over.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The club operates across several communes in the Provence Verte: Tourves, Bras and Cuers, with trails suited to running with your dog.</p>
